# Monochromatic Color Palette Rules

## Core Colors

- **Background Colors**
  ```typescript
  // ✅ DO: Use these background colors
  "bg-white"          // Primary background
  "bg-gray-50"        // Subtle background, hover states
  "bg-gray-100"       // Stronger background, active states
  "bg-gray-900"       // Dark background for contrast (e.g., buttons)
  
  // ❌ DON'T: Use transparent backgrounds or other colors
  "bg-transparent"    // Avoid transparent backgrounds
  "bg-zinc-*"        // Avoid zinc or other gray variants
  "bg-black"         // Use gray-900 instead
  ```

- **Text Colors**
  ```typescript
  // ✅ DO: Use these text colors
  "text-gray-900"     // Primary text
  "text-gray-700"     // Secondary text
  "text-gray-600"     // Tertiary text
  "text-gray-500"     // Muted text
  "text-gray-400"     // Extra muted text
  
  // ❌ DON'T: Use other color variants
  "text-zinc-*"      // Avoid zinc variants
  "text-black"       // Use gray-900 instead
  ```

- **Border Colors**
  ```typescript
  // ✅ DO: Use these border colors
  "border-gray-200"   // Primary border
  "border-gray-300"   // Stronger border
  
  // ❌ DON'T: Use other border colors
  "border-zinc-*"    // Avoid zinc variants
  ```

## Component-Specific Rules

### Dropdowns
- **Content Background**: Must be solid white with a border
  ```typescript
  // ✅ DO:
  "bg-white border border-gray-200 shadow-md"
  
  // ❌ DON'T:
  "bg-popover"       // Avoid semantic colors
  "bg-transparent"   // Never use transparent backgrounds
  ```

- **Items**:
  ```typescript
  // ✅ DO:
  "hover:bg-gray-50"  // Hover state
  "text-gray-700"     // Default text
  "text-gray-900"     // Active text
  
  // ❌ DON'T:
  "hover:bg-accent"   // Avoid semantic colors
  "focus:bg-accent"   // Use gray scale instead
  ```

### Modals/Dialogs
- **Overlay**: Semi-transparent dark background
  ```typescript
  // ✅ DO:
  "bg-gray-900/50"    // 50% opacity black overlay
  
  // ❌ DON'T:
  "bg-black/50"       // Avoid pure black
  ```

- **Content**: Solid white background with border
  ```typescript
  // ✅ DO:
  "bg-white border border-gray-200 shadow-xl"
  
  // ❌ DON'T:
  "bg-background"     // Avoid semantic colors
  ```

### Buttons
- **Primary**:
  ```typescript
  // ✅ DO:
  "bg-gray-900 text-white hover:bg-gray-800"
  
  // ❌ DON'T:
  "bg-primary"       // Avoid semantic colors
  ```

- **Secondary/Outline**:
  ```typescript
  // ✅ DO:
  "border-gray-200 hover:bg-gray-50 text-gray-700"
  
  // ❌ DON'T:
  "border-input"     // Avoid semantic colors
  ```

## Implementation Notes

1. **Consistency**: Always use the same color values for similar UI elements
2. **Accessibility**: Ensure sufficient contrast between text and background
3. **Hover States**: Use lighter grays (gray-50, gray-100) for hover effects
4. **Shadows**: Use shadows to create depth instead of different background colors
5. **Dark Mode**: Currently not supported - remove all dark mode classes

## Examples

### Dropdown Menu
```typescript
// ✅ DO:
<DropdownMenuContent className="bg-white border border-gray-200 shadow-md">
  <DropdownMenuItem className="text-gray-700 hover:bg-gray-50 hover:text-gray-900">
    Item
  </DropdownMenuItem>
</DropdownMenuContent>

// ❌ DON'T:
<DropdownMenuContent className="bg-popover">
  <DropdownMenuItem className="hover:bg-accent">
    Item
  </DropdownMenuItem>
</DropdownMenuContent>
```

### Modal/Dialog
```typescript
// ✅ DO:
<Dialog>
  <DialogOverlay className="bg-gray-900/50" />
  <DialogContent className="bg-white border border-gray-200 shadow-xl">
    <DialogTitle className="text-gray-900">Title</DialogTitle>
    <DialogDescription className="text-gray-600">Description</DialogDescription>
  </DialogContent>
</Dialog>

// ❌ DON'T:
<Dialog>
  <DialogOverlay className="bg-black/50" />
  <DialogContent className="bg-background">
    <DialogTitle className="text-foreground">Title</DialogTitle>
    <DialogDescription className="text-muted-foreground">Description</DialogDescription>
  </DialogContent>
</Dialog>
```